### PHP-Writing

- Never grow the static analyzer's baseline to get a clean run; fix the new error, or suppress it narrowly with a *why* comment.
<!-- Project-specific / PHP-Writing -->

### PHP-Security

- Expose only the web document root (conventionally `public/`: the front controller and static files) to the web server; keep source, configuration, `vendor/`, and `.env` files outside it.
- Never pass untrusted input to `unserialize()`, whatever its `allowed_classes` option: instantiating and autoloading classes can run code; exchange such data as JSON (`json_decode()`).
